+## Form submission
+
+The text shown in the input is formatted for display, so it is not what a form should send. When the input has a `name`, the datepicker moves that name to a hidden `<input>` inserted before it and keeps it updated with the selected date(s) in `YYYY-MM-DD` format, the same value a native `<input type="date">` submits. The visible input only shows the formatted date.
+
+```html
+<!-- What you write -->
+<input type="text" class="form-control" name="start" data-bs-toggle="datepicker" value="2026-06-10">
+
+<!-- What the JS creates -->
+<input type="hidden" name="start" value="2026-06-10">
+<input type="text" class="form-control" data-bs-toggle="datepicker" value="6/10/2026">
+```
+
+For multiple dates and date ranges, the hidden input holds a comma-separated list, for example `2026-06-10,2026-06-18`. A date typed into the input is mirrored into the hidden input; text that is not a date submits an empty value.
+
+The instance is created when the input receives focus, so an input that is never focused submits its `value` attribute unchanged. Use the `YYYY-MM-DD` format for prefilled values.
+
 ## Dark mode
 
 The datepicker automatically adapts to Bootstrap’s color modes. When `data-bs-theme="dark"` is set on a parent element or the `<html>` tag, the calendar popup inherits that theme.
